Faster 2D textures, depth clears and colour material, same pixels

- swrast/s_triangle.c: the fast textured spans skip the double multiply by
  1/q when it is exactly 1 (2D and orthographic drawing, and GL_FASTEST
  segments): (float) (s * 1.0) is s itself.
- swrast/s_depth.c: 24-bit depth buffers without stencil (Z24_X8, what
  EGL, SDL and GLUT use) are cleared with a plain fill (a memset when the
  three depth bytes match, as for 1.0 and 0.0), not a read, mask and
  write per value; the unused byte is never read.
- tnl/t_vb_light.c: with GL_COLOR_MATERIAL, the derived light/material
  values are worked out again only when a vertex's colour differs from
  the last one's (compared bit for bit, as words), not for every vertex.

Every picture is unchanged: the rendering checks give the same hashes, and
every glbench scene's colour and depth match the previous build exactly.

